      "problem": "What is the common difference for the following arithmetic sequence?\n\n$$\n-5,\\,-12,\\,-19,\\,-26,\\,…\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The common difference $d$ of an arithmetic sequence is the difference between any two consecutive terms.\n\nTherefore, the common difference for our sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-12-(-5) \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
